Q. explain what is outofmemory error?


“OutOfMemoryError is an Error thrown by the JVM when it cannot allocate the memory required for an operation or 
when a required JVM memory area cannot provide enough memory. The most common case is OutOfMemoryError: 
Java heap space, which occurs when the JVM cannot allocate an object in the heap because sufficient heap memory is unavailable.

It can happen because the application is genuinely using more memory than the configured limit,
because objects are being retained unnecessarily and causing a memory leak, or because the application has an unusually high allocation rate.

Unlike normal exceptions, OutOfMemoryError represents a serious JVM resource-exhaustion condition
so applications generally should not try to recover from it simply by catching the error. Instead,
we investigate heap usage, object retention, GC behavior, and JVM memory configuration.”


